course: dictionary
lesson: 14600
title: Abbreviations: am, pm and PM
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «pm» is a short form of the Latin words post meridiem, which mean "after midday". So 3 pm is three o'clock in the afternoon: it is after 12 noon and before midnight.
explain: When you work out how long something takes, count across noon. «The club runs from 10 am to 2 pm.» That is 4 hours: 2 hours up to noon, then 2 more hours after noon.
explain: Capital letters and context tell you which meaning is right. «The PM spoke on the news tonight» means Prime Minister, the leader of the government. «Send me a PM after school» means send a private message online. Look at the words around it to decide.
fact: «pm» is an abbreviation, a short form of the Latin words post meridiem, meaning "after midday".
fact: «pm» means the hours after 12 noon and before midnight, such as 3 pm.
fact: 12 pm is noon (midday), and 12 am is midnight. Many people mix these two up.
fact: «PM» can stand for Prime Minister, the leader of the government, in countries such as the UK, Australia and Canada.
fact: Online, «PM» or «PM me» means a private message, sent to one person only.
exercise: «The shop opens at 9 am and closes at 5 pm.» What does pm mean here? | *The hours after 12 noon and before midnight | The hours before 12 noon | The Prime Minister | A private message
exercise: «The PM gave a speech on the news tonight.» What does PM stand for here? | *Prime Minister | Private message | Post meridiem | Pet monkey
exercise: Jun says, «Send me a PM after school!» What does PM mean? | *A private message online | The Prime Minister | A pumpkin muffin | 3 pm exactly
test: «The train leaves at 4 pm.» What time of day is 4 pm? | Midnight | *In the afternoon | Just before midday | Early morning
test: What time is the same as 12 noon? | *12 pm | 12 midnight in the morning, just after 12 am | 12 am | 1 am
exam: «The class starts at 15:00 on the 24-hour clock.» What is this time in pm? | 3 am | *3 pm | 1 pm | 12 pm
